WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.988
On the fixtures, Microsoft 365 gives six
notices: a retirement with a provider date,

2
00:00:05.988 --> 00:00:09.568
a change the kit marks
action required by its rule,

3
00:00:09.568 --> 00:00:12.013
three advisories and an incident.

4
00:00:12.013 --> 00:00:14.762
The next capture shows the
difference that matters.

5
00:00:14.762 --> 00:00:19.806
The retirement of basic authentication
for SMTP client submission is action

6
00:00:19.806 --> 00:00:24.462
required because Microsoft said so,
in its action-required-by date field.

7
00:00:24.462 --> 00:00:27.826
The SharePoint Framework change
is action required because

8
00:00:27.826 --> 00:00:30.662
of a stated kit rule about
a message center category.

9
00:00:30.662 --> 00:00:32.063
The record says which,

10
00:00:32.063 --> 00:00:36.263
so nobody argues with Microsoft
about a date Microsoft never set.

11
00:00:36.263 --> 00:00:39.652
This gate supports the same
two controls as gate one,

12
00:00:39.652 --> 00:00:44.775
plus configuration change control: a
change Microsoft announces is reviewed,

13
00:00:44.775 --> 00:00:47.376
with an impact analysis, before it lands.

14
00:00:47.376 --> 00:00:51.700
Until the reader exists, Learn's
own cmdlet lists the same posts.

15
00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:55.490
And there's nothing to roll
back: the collection only reads.
